# A throwaway self-signed certificate + key for 127.0.0.1, used by
# tests/test_download.py to stand up a real HTTPS server no root store trusts.
# It is a test fixture, not a secret: it grants nothing, is trusted nowhere, and
# the test's whole point is that verifying it FAILS. Generated 2026-08-23 with
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout key.pem -out cert.pem -days 36500 \
#     -nodes -subj "/CN=localhost" -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:localhost,IP:127.0.0.1"
# Valid until 2126; after that it fails verification as "certificate has expired"
# instead of "self-signed certificate", which is still the answer the test asserts.
